From ab8d9bb45db393ff59efe03523acb6efa76f03f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:15:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): key annotation caches on a content revision,
 not board file stats [daveey]

The session-list annotation's count fingerprint, per-board read memo and remote-links fingerprint were keyed
on each board file's stat. On David-MBP bookkeeping writes the annotation never reads (kanban_sync_state
stamps, kanban_dispatch_stamp, replica pull stamps) moved that key ~61x/min, so every sidebar poll re-read the
boards and re-projected the links (example-card, part of example-card).

- kanban_activity_revision: a one-row counter bumped by triggers (installed at connect init) on insert/delete
  and on updates of read columns of the tables the readers read (boards: tasks, task_links, task_runs,
  task_events, task_comments, kanban_notify_subs, task_chat_links; replicas: tasks, task_chat_links).
  Claim/lease/heartbeat/sync/notifier-inflight columns are bookkeeping. Same-transaction triggers keep
  read-your-writes. Readers fall back to the stat when any watched table lacks its triggers.
- _activity_fingerprint and _board_memo use that key; replica link rows are memoized on it; _ledger_owners
  is memoized on the projection's card identity.
- An equal recompute keeps the published objects and _read_annotation_parts returns the previous frozen
  parts, skipping freeze/copy work.

Mac replay on DB copies (120 s, ~57 bookkeeping + 3 task writes/min, 1 poll/s): process CPU 3152 -> 1252
ms/min, board reads 65 -> 6, poll p50 31 -> 10 ms.
